       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin in adults. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the labeled maximum.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day in total:** for example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 to 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals:** a typical starting or maintenance range.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm the intended total daily dose, and I'll enter it right away. If this is a new start, I'd also suggest titrating up gradually."
